//! The orchestration verbs, as decision logic both seams share (nxf epic 6j6v.qvfp, spec
//! `docs/specs/E5c-chat-orchestration-api.md`).
//!
//! These verbs used to live in `cli.rs`, module-private, and resolved their inputs from ambient
//! process state: `actor()`/`origin()`/`session()`/`hop()`/`resolve_now()` read `NXC_*`,
//! the declaration directory was walked up from the workspace, `select_worker()` read
//! `NXC_WORKER`/`NXC_SIDECAR`.
//! That is fine for a process-per-invocation CLI and impossible for a library — a host serves many
//! actors from one process and owns its own clock, identity and sidecar path.
//!
//! So the bodies moved HERE and take all of it explicitly via [`Ctx`]. `cli.rs` is now the adapter
//! that fills a `Ctx` from the environment, and [`crate::engine::Engine`] fills one from explicit
//! arguments plus injected [`Definitions`]. One implementation, two seams — which is also why the
//! `tests/parity.rs` differential can hold them to each other at all. Copying the verbs onto the
//! handle instead would have created a second implementation of the depth guard, the
//! preflight-before-persist order, the bare-vs-qualified handle split and the completion routing,
//! every one of which has already cost a fix round.
//!
//! **The seam adds no new semantics**: `now`/`actor`/`origin` arrive from outside the verbs, and
//! everything derived from them is derived identically to how the CLI derives it. WHO supplies them
//! differs by adapter and, since nxf 6j6v.07me, mostly is not the caller any more — the CLI reads
//! `NXC_*`, the handle answers `origin` for itself, resolves `actor` from the session map and
//! defaults `now` to the clock. [`Caller`] is what is left over: who is calling, and nothing that
//! can be derived from that.

